<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Idle reaper: one tick every 15 minutes, with no Claude session as its parent.

  The operator's rule (2026-11-07, restated 2026-11-10): a headless worker idle for 15 minutes
  exits. `reap-idle-headless.py` shipped as the close verb, but no command, step, agent or
  plist ever called it. This job is that missing caller.

  WHY A LAUNCHD AGENT, and not a slash command or an in-session `Monitor`:

    * A slash command is started by a human, and the rule is meant to hold with nobody watching.
    * An in-session `Monitor` dies with its session, so the reap would stop exactly when the
      idle population is largest.
    * `StartInterval` gives a FRESH PROCESS per tick, so there is no loop to die. Same shape
      as `com.bborbe.rebase-agent`.

  WHY NOT `com.bborbe.fleet-keeper`: that job is report-only by operator decision
  (2026-11-01, card efc771fb) after it killed the Fleet Manager twice, and
  `scripts/tests/test_fleet_keeper.py` pins it against every kill path. A reaper on that
  clock would undo the decision. This job is separate so the two stay distinguishable in
  `launchctl` and in their logs.

  The cadence is 900 s. Measured from the moment a worker turns idle, the close lands between
  15 and 30 minutes later.

  ⚠️ WHAT THIS JOB DOES: it SIGTERMs live `claude` processes. That is its purpose and the
  reason installing it is an operator step. It closes the PROCESS only: the transcript and the
  task's `claude_session_id` survive, so a parked worker can be resumed later. Each candidate
  first passes the reaper's eleven guards (busy, wrapper state, open card, live watcher, task
  state, …); every refusal is final for that tick and is logged with its token.

  Install:
    cp launchd/com.bborbe.idle-reaper.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$UID ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.bborbe.idle-reaper.plist

  Stop it (the reap halts at once; nothing else depends on it):
    launchctl bootout gui/$UID/com.bborbe.idle-reaper

  Reload after an upgrade:
    launchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.bborbe.idle-reaper

  The script path is the marketplace clone, not a version-pinned cache dir, for the same
  reason `fleet-keeper` uses it: a cache path would pin the agent to one release and
  silently run stale code after every upgrade.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.bborbe.idle-reaper</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/usr/local/bin/python3</string>
        <string>/Users/bborbe/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/claude-supervisor/scripts/idle-reaper-tick.py</string>
    </array>

    <!--
      launchd gives a job no login shell, so it never reads ~/.zshrc, and anything not on
      this list is simply not found.

      ⚠️ `~/.local/bin` is load-bearing, and a missing entry does not show up as an error.
      Both verbs resolve a session's task through `vault-cli config list`, which lives in
      ~/.local/bin. Without it the call raises FileNotFoundError, `_vault_config()` swallows
      that into an empty config, and EVERY candidate reads `task-unresolved`. The reaper and
      `close-worker.py` then refuse everything and the log looks like normal refusals.
      Measured 2026-11-10 on one live session: `task-not-terminal` from a login shell,
      `task-unresolved` under `PATH=/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin`, and `task-not-terminal`
      again once ~/.local/bin was added.

      The rest: `ps` (/bin), `pgrep` (/usr/bin) and `git` (/usr/bin), all measured.
      ~/.local/bin comes last, so a binary dropped there cannot shadow a system tool.
    -->
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin:/Users/bborbe/.local/bin</string>
    </dict>

    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>900</integer>

    <!--
      Not at load: the first tick waits a full interval. Installing the job should not
      SIGTERM anything on the spot. A deliberate first run is
      `launchctl kickstart gui/$UID/com.bborbe.idle-reaper`.
    -->
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/bborbe/Library/Logs/idle-reaper.log</string>

    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/bborbe/Library/Logs/idle-reaper.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
